{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"no\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"To investigate the role of the STN neural activity in gait freezing we compared the STN oscillations between (effective) walking and ongoing freezing episodes. We first studied power changes in low frequency (i.e. θ-α rhythms) and in the β-frequency band of the two STN and did not find any differences during gait freezing in comparison to (effective) walking (Fig. 3A and B).\",\n    \"Despite the lack of subthalamic activity changes during gait freezing in our study, exaggerated STN β-synchronization may still influence dynamic motor processing in favour of gait freezing development (Anidi et al., 2018).\",\n    \"The spectral analysis was performed between 4 Hz and 80 Hz, with a resolution of 1 Hz.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"To study the cortical-subthalamic and the interhemispheric subthalamic coupling, we computed the cross power spectral density (CPSD) between the LFP signals of the cortical areas and the STN, as well as between the two STN (Shine et al., 2014; Canessa et al., 2016).\",\n    \"To assess for differences in the cortico-subcortical coupling across the five conditions, we integrated the CPSD in the specific θ-α band, obtaining an index (θαCCCX/STNk) to describe the cross coupling between each cortical region of interest [CX = (SMA+/–, M1+/–, PC+/–, TC+/–)] and its own ipsilateral STN for all epochs k = {Walking, FPRE, FSTART, FSTOP, FPOST}.\",\n    \"We showed that during (effective) walking the cortex and the STN were coupled in a low frequency band (i.e. θ-α rhythms). In contrast, gait freezing was characterized by a low frequency cortical-subthalamic decoupling in the hemisphere with less striatal dopaminergic innervation (H−) (Fig. 4A).\",\n    \"During gait freezing (FSTART – FSTOP), the cortex and the STN decoupled selectively in the hemisphere with less striatal dopamine (H−).\",\n    \"The disruption of this cortical-subcortical coupling anticipated and specifically characterized the freezing episodes, to recover when the effective walking pattern was regained (Fig. 4A).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法与全文不符。论文明确区分了STN局部振荡功率（power）和皮层-STN跨脑区耦合（coupling）。对于前者，研究者直接比较了步行与冻结期间双侧STN的低频θ-α功率，明确报告没有显著差异；讨论部分也再次确认缺乏STN局部活动变化。因此，该文不能作为支持「STN局部theta/delta状态转换异常机制」的直接证据。对于后者，论文明确报告步行时皮层与STN存在4–13 Hz θ-α频段耦合，而冻结发生前及冻结期间，低频皮层-STN耦合发生解耦，并在步行恢复后恢复。指控者关于论文主要发现是皮层-STN θ-α耦合变化、而非STN局部θ功率变化的描述有全文依据。两者是不同的神经生理指标，不能将跨脑区耦合变化直接等同于STN局部功率变化。另需注意，论文分析的目标低频段为4–13 Hz θ-α频段，并未提供STN局部δ频段状态转换异常的证据。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "0d319a58-a50c-4c9f-bbb7-65cb990e0674", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T070530936201Z", "elapsed_seconds": 39.203, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T07:06:10.141985+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "f8cd11f5d0e44212ade585bb33d8cd2824aa44dd83c8ac48b5de3261edf83c1c", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T070530936201Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "6a2104ca298e333f7029a4c1d5c86cef7e24a3df6003ed127190ff3794d22ea0"}}}
